## Why This Is Asked
The question probes realistic streaming test coverage, including latency, durability, and recovery under failures.

## Key Concepts
- End-to-end testing for streaming pipelines
- Backpressure and lag metrics
- Idempotent sinks and deduplication
- Fault injection chaos testing
- Reproducible test data and replay

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo test hook: dedupe by (id, partition)
function isDuplicate(evt, seen){
  const key = evt.id + ':' + evt.partition;
  if (seen.has(key)) return true;
  seen.add(key); return false;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you instrument end-to-end latency measurement across microservices?
- How would you design test data generators reflecting real-world distributions?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses practical testing of async, fault-tolerant workflows and how beginners wire tests across layers.

## Key Concepts
- Async pipelines, at-least-once vs dedup
- Idempotency, deduplication IDs
- Retries/backoff, fault injection
- Test types: unit/integration/e2e

## Code Example
```javascript
// naive dedup example
function process(msg, store){
  if (store.seen(msg.id)) return;
  // process
  store.markSeen(msg.id);
}
```

